5. MAP ARCHITECTURE

Do not hard-code the application to one map provider.

Create a map abstraction.

For example:

interface MapProvider {
  renderMap(): Promise<void>
  searchPlaces(query: string): Promise<PlaceResult[]>
  geocode(query: string): Promise<GeoPoint | null>
  reverseGeocode(point: GeoPoint): Promise<PlaceResult | null>
  getRoute(points: GeoPoint[]): Promise<RouteResult>
  getDistance(from: GeoPoint, to: GeoPoint): Promise<number>
}

The UI must not directly depend on Google Maps or another provider.

The provider must be replaceable later.

Use PostGIS for geographic database operations.

---

6. LANGUAGES

The application supports from the beginning:

Arabic
French
English

Arabic:

RTL

French / English:

LTR

Implement i18n from the beginning.

Do not hard-code user-facing strings throughout components.

Language selection must be persistent.

