39. POSTGRES / POSTGIS

Enable:

CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS postgis;

Use:

GEOGRAPHY(POINT, 4326)

for locations.

Add appropriate indexes:

GIST(location)

and indexes for:

trip status
departure_at
driver_id
client_id
booking status
segment trip_id
checkpoint trip_id
notifications user_id
payments booking_id

Use composite indexes where query patterns justify them.

---

40. CONSTRAINTS

Implement database constraints for critical invariants.

Examples:

vehicle capacity > 0
seats > 0
price >= 0
rating BETWEEN 1 AND 5
sequence >= 0
reserved_seats >= 0
reserved_seats <= capacity

Use foreign keys.

Use unique constraints where logically required.

Use check constraints for business invariants that belong in the database.

---

41. ROW LEVEL SECURITY

Enable RLS on all user-facing tables.

Principle:

«Users must only access data they are authorized to access.»

Examples:

profiles

User:

read own profile
update own profile

Admin:

read/update all

Role must not be self-modifiable.

verification_documents

Owner:

read own documents
upload own documents

Admin:

read/review all

trips

Authenticated users:

read published trips

Driver:

manage own trips

but only if verified where required.

bookings

Client:

read own bookings

Driver:

read bookings belonging to own trips

Admin:

full access

payments

Client:

read own payment records

Admin:

full access

Driver should not receive unnecessary sensitive payment-provider information.

notifications

Only owner can read/update their notifications.

audit_logs

Admin only.

Never rely solely on frontend authorization.

---

42. STORAGE

Create at minimum:

avatars
verification-documents

Recommended:

avatars
    → public or controlled public access

verification-documents
    → private

Identity documents must never be publicly accessible.

Use signed URLs where appropriate.

---

43. RPC / TRANSACTIONAL OPERATIONS

Create secure PostgreSQL functions/RPCs for operations that must be atomic.

At minimum:

create_trip
publish_trip
search_trips
create_booking
confirm_booking
reject_booking
cancel_booking
create_resale
buy_resale
request_transfer
approve_transfer
reject_transfer

The exact RPC names can be improved if necessary, but preserve a clean domain-oriented API.

Critical RPCs must use transactions and row locking.

---

44. SECURITY MODEL

Never trust:

frontend role
frontend price
frontend seat availability
frontend payment status
frontend user ID

Validate everything server-side.

The client must never be able to:

change its role
mark a payment as paid
increase vehicle capacity arbitrarily after bookings
bypass seat availability
change another user's booking
approve its own verification
modify audit logs

