53. LOADING / EMPTY STATES

Every major data view must support:

loading
success
empty
error

Examples:

No trips found
No upcoming bookings
No notifications
No pending verification documents
No transfer requests

---

54. REALTIME

Use Supabase Realtime only where it provides real value.

Good candidates:

booking request status
notifications
driver approval
transfer status
payment state where safe
trip operational status

Do not make every database table realtime.

---

55. PERFORMANCE

Optimize for mobile networks.

Requirements:

- lazy-load routes/pages
- paginate large lists
- avoid unnecessary realtime subscriptions
- debounce search
- use database-side filtering
- use indexed queries
- use PostGIS indexes
- avoid loading all trips into the browser
- avoid loading all places unnecessarily

Search must happen server-side.

---

56. DATABASE QUERY PRINCIPLES

Never retrieve the whole dataset and filter in JavaScript.

Bad:

SELECT all trips
↓
filter in browser

Good:

PostgreSQL/PostGIS query
↓
only return matching trips

Use RPC for complex route matching.

---

57. API / SERVICE LAYER

The frontend should not scatter raw Supabase queries everywhere.

Create typed service modules such as:

tripService
bookingService
paymentService
resaleService
transferService
notificationService
profileService
adminService

Each service should expose clear domain operations.

Example:

bookingService.createBooking(...)
bookingService.cancelBooking(...)
transferService.requestTransfer(...)
resaleService.createListing(...)

